MiniFASNet PAD — Strobe-Differential Liveness Model
====================================================

Model id: minifasnet_pad
Source: Self-trained on physics-based synthetic strobe-differential data
Licence: Apache-2.0 (code reference: Silent-Face Anti-Spoofing)

Provenance
----------

The ONNX weights (49 KB, ~80K parameters) were trained from scratch on
physics-based synthetic strobe-differential data encoding the signals
described in the Nam-tor design spec section 6.4:

  - 1/r^2 falloff for live faces (inverse-square distance cue)
  - Specular hotspot from the IR emitter (live skin reflectance)
  - Subsurface scattering simulation (live tissue)
  - Near-zero differential D = On - Off for screen replay attacks
  - Weak/flat differential for print attacks
  - Uniform differential for cutout attacks

No licence-restricted dataset was used to derive these weights. The
training data is entirely synthetic, generated from first-principles
physics models. The training recipe is in ml/recipes/train_pad.py.

Code Reference
--------------

The network architecture (MiniFASNet) is adapted from Silent-Face
Anti-Spoofing (https://github.com/minivision-ai/Silent-Face-Anti-Spoofing),
which is licensed under Apache-2.0. Only the architectural design was
referenced; the weights are independently trained.

